              "id": "F1",
              "kind": "claimed_speedup",
              "family": "empty cookie header",
              "why": "The change returns a literal `{}` immediately for an empty header, avoiding the initial `cookies = {}` allocation in the original code. The maintainer likely believed this saves a dict allocation on the common case of no cookies.",
              "size_meaning": "n is ignored – the input is always the empty string.",
              "make_source": "def make(n):\n    # n is ignored; we always return a single empty header\n    return [[\"\"]]",
              "example_args": [],
              "origin": "plan",
              "screen_ratio": 1.0198499302735753,
              "valid_fraction": 1.0,
              "error": null
            },
            {
              "id": "F2",
              "kind": "suspected_slowdown",
              "family": "many cookies (n cookies)",
              "why": "For a non‑empty header the new version creates **two** dictionaries (`{}` on the early return path is dead code, then `cookies = {}` again before the loop) and calls `strip()` on each cookie *twice* (once in the original `strip().split()` and now explicitly). The extra dict allocation and the extra `strip()` call grow linearly with the number of cookies, so runtime increases with n.",
              "size_meaning": "n = number of `name=value` pairs in the header.",
              "make_source": "def make(n):\n    # build a header like \"c0=v0; c1=v1; ...; c{n-1}=v{n-1}\"\n    parts = [f\"c{i}=v{i}\" for i in range(n)]\n    header = \"; \".join(parts)\n    return [[header]]",
              "example_args": [],
              "origin": "plan",
              "screen_ratio": 1.0129782348120757,
              "valid_fraction": 1.0,
              "error": null
            },
            {
              "id": "F3",
              "kind": "suspected_slowdown",
              "family": "cookies surrounded by whitespace",
              "why": "The new code executes `cookie = cookie.strip()` for every split fragment *before* the `=` test, while the old version only stripped when `=` was present (`cookie.strip().split(...)`). Headers that contain many fragments without `=` (e.g. stray spaces or malformed tokens) pay the `strip()` cost without any benefit, slowing the path that the change was supposed to accelerate.",
              "size_meaning": "n = number of whitespace‑only fragments plus one real cookie.",
              "make_source": "def make(n):\n    # n‑1 fragments that are just spaces, then one valid cookie\n    fragments = [\"   \" for _ in range(n-1)] + [\"session=abc123\"]\n    header = \";\".join(fragments)\n    return [[header]]",
              "example_args": [],
              "origin": "plan",
              "screen_ratio": 1.078432455096426,
              "valid_fraction": 1.0,
              "error": null
            },
            {
